sentences.l:
for I go to Sparta and to sandy Pylos,
of my father's homecoming to inquire, long gone,
if some mortal may tell me, or a rumor I may hear
from Zeus, which most of all brings report to men;

let no longer any ready-minded, gentle and kind sceptre-holding king be,
nor knowing in his mind what is fitting,
but let him always be harsh, and do reckless things;

not even so would his wife rejoice, longing for it though she does,
at his coming, but he would there meet an unseemly fate,
if he should fight against greater numbers;

“Telemachus, not hereafter will you be base, nor witless,
if indeed your father's noble force has been instilled in you —
such a man was he, to bring to pass both deed and word;
